## What Works Today

1) PCI USB controller discovery and classification
- Detects class/subclass USB PCI functions.
- Classifies by prog-if to UHCI/OHCI/EHCI/xHCI.
- Captures vendor/device IDs, BAR0, IRQ, and controller metadata.

2) Backend split with common host-controller contract
- usb_hc_ops dispatches probe/reset/halt/start/scan_ports/service_ports plus optional desc8/desc18/config/set-config EP0 hooks.
- All four backend files provide real implementations for those stages.

3) Guarded lifecycle sequencing
- Core executes probe -> reset -> halt -> start.
- Tracks attempts/success/failure counters and degraded state.

4) Root-hub port scan and service
- scan_ports captures connect/change bitmaps.
- service_ports applies per-port reset/enable handling.
- Speed masks are populated (low/full/high/super depending on backend rules).

5) Candidate-device synthesis and address bookkeeping scaffold
- Core creates candidate rows with hc/kind/port/present/enabled/speed.
- Per-controller address allocator state exists (1..127).
- Per-port generation tracking exists for change epochs.

6) Observability
- /proc/usb exports controller counts, states, lifecycle counters, scan/service counters, root-port masks, candidate rows, and device-model enumeration rows/counters.

7) xHCI EP0 descriptor vertical-slice start
- xHCI backend now provides a first synchronous EP0 path for `GET_DESCRIPTOR(Device, 8)`.
- xHCI backend now also provides synchronous `GET_DESCRIPTOR(Device, 18)`.
- xHCI backend now also provides synchronous `GET_DESCRIPTOR(Configuration)` reads.
- xHCI backend now also provides synchronous `SET_CONFIGURATION`.
- Core consumes these hooks and tracks `desc8_ok`/`desc18_ok`, `addr_set`, and parsed device identity.

8) Endpoint capability persistence and attach dispatch
- Core now records a bounded endpoint capability table from config descriptors.
- `/proc/usb` `udevN` rows now include per-endpoint capability tuples and attach attempt/result counters.
- Core now calls first class-driver attach hooks for known USB scaffolds.

9) Attach lifecycle hardening for churn
- Device slot selection now retires stale same-port prior generations and reuses inactive slots.
- Class attach dispatch now skips duplicate attach calls when the configured identity signature is unchanged.
- `/proc/usb` now reports global attach dedup and retire counters.

10) Policy-gated attach and explicit detach callbacks
- USB core now gates class attach attempts through driver matchers plus interface/endpoint policy checks.
- USB core now calls class detach hooks on slot retirement (`rtl815x_usb_detach`, `wpan_usb_detach`).
- rtl815x/wpan scaffolds now expose `*_usb_match` and `*_usb_detach` hooks and track active vs seen probes in proc summaries.

11) Descriptor-accurate routing and rebind reconciliation
- USB core policy now selects candidate interfaces from parsed interface descriptors (bounded table) rather than relying on first-interface heuristics.
- Endpoint capability entries now carry interface association, enabling per-interface endpoint policy checks.
- Attach signature now includes selected interface identity + endpoint signature and triggers detach/rebind on drift.

12) Driver-owned bind context contract
- `rtl815x_usb_attach` / `wpan_usb_attach` now allocate and return bind handles to USB core.
- `rtl815x_usb_detach` / `wpan_usb_detach` now consume bind handles, avoiding ambiguous detach among same VID:PID devices.
- USB core now stores and surfaces attach handle state per `udev` row.

## What Is Missing

1) No transfer engine
- No active URB/TRB/QH/qTD/ED/TD scheduling path.
- No generalized ring/schedule framework for broad USB traffic (current xHCI path is narrow bootstrap logic for descriptor reads).

2) Incomplete protocol enumeration state machine
- Initial xHCI endpoint-0 desc8+desc18+config descriptor reads and `SET_CONFIGURATION` exist, but endpoint activation/transfer scheduling is still incomplete.
- Descriptor-derived stable object graph (device/interface/endpoint) is still incomplete.

3) No runtime hotplug loop
- Current path is init-time orchestration in usb_init.
- No long-lived interrupt/poll event path for connect/disconnect churn.

4) Class-driver handoff is still scaffold-level
- USB core now has descriptor-aware policy gating, explicit detach callbacks, rebind-on-signature-drift, and handle-based bind identity, but it still lacks full class-driver transport datapaths.

5) No production class datapath on USB
- rtl815x and ieee802154 paths are explicit scaffolds and proc visibility only.

