## Practical Next Step

Immediate best next implementation target is transport bring-up on top of the new bind contract:
- Expand interface-policy support for composite devices (multi-altsetting and class-specific companion descriptors).
- Add bind-handle backed per-driver context blocks (endpoint selection, interface index, device speed snapshot).
- Start first control/bulk path stubs in rtl815x using selected interface and endpoint mapping.

Follow-up target after that:
- Convert parsed endpoint inventory into class-match inputs so USB class-driver handoff can start.

That sequence is the shortest path to a true attach-ready USB core and the remaining jump toward ~55% maturity.
